            <ArticleTitle>Painful Traumatic Trigeminal Neuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>371-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.coms.2016.03.002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1042-3699(16)00007-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article discusses neuropathic pain of traumatic origin affecting the trigeminal nerve. This syndrome has been termed painful traumatic trigeminal neuropathy by the International Headache Society and replaces atypical odontalgia, deafferentation pain, traumatic neuropathy, and phantom toothache. The discussion emphasizes the diagnosis and the early and late management of injuries to the trigeminal nerve and subsequent painful conditions.</AbstractText>
